      "message": "Once you address the other comments, we\u0027re ready for unit tests!\n\nHere is Gemini generated code to get you started. Make sure that it compiles and that the tests pass in your chroot.\n\n----\n\n### Step 1: Create the Basic Test File (`util/focaltech/focaltech_test.cc`)\n\nCreate `util/focaltech/focaltech_test.cc`. This test verifies math rounding macros, error string mapping, help string definitions, and SCSI CDB block generation (`BuildFtCmd`). Including an explicit `main()` ensures compatibility with `pkg-config`.\n\n```c\n/* Copyright 2026 The ChromiumOS Authors\n * Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be\n * found in the LICENSE file.\n */\n#include \u003cgtest/gtest.h\u003e\n\n#include \u003carray\u003e\n#include \u003ccstdint\u003e\n#include \u003cstring_view\u003e\n\n#include \"ft_help.h\"\n#include \"ft_scsi.h\"\n#include \"ft_util.h\"\n\nnamespace {\n\n// 1. Test ft_util.h (Math utilities \u0026 Error string mapping)\nTEST(FtUtilTest, DivRoundUp) {\n  EXPECT_EQ(FtDivRoundUp(10, 3), 4);\n  EXPECT_EQ(FtDivRoundUp(9, 3), 3);\n  EXPECT_EQ(FtDivRoundUp(0, 10), 0);\n  EXPECT_EQ(FtDivRoundUp(4096, 4096), 1);\n}\n\nTEST(FtUtilTest, ToStringMapping) {\n  EXPECT_EQ(ToString(FtError::kSuccess), \"Success\");\n  EXPECT_EQ(ToString(FtError::kNoSuchDevice), \"No such device\");\n  EXPECT_EQ(ToString(FtError::kParameterError), \"Parameter error\");\n  EXPECT_EQ(ToString(FtError::kNoSuchFile), \"No such file\");\n  EXPECT_EQ(ToString(FtError::kResultFail), \"Result fail\");\n  EXPECT_EQ(ToString(FtError::kInvalidMode), \"Invalid mode\");\n}\n\n// 2. Test ft_help.h (Help String Definition)\nTEST(FtHelpTest, HelpStringNotEmpty) {\n  EXPECT_FALSE(ft_help::kCmdHelpString.empty());\n  EXPECT_NE(ft_help::kCmdHelpString.find(\"Usage:\"), std::string_view::npos);\n}\n\n// 3. Test ft_scsi.h (SCSI Command CDB Building)\nTEST(FtScsiTest, BuildFtCmdBasic) {\n  // BuildFtCmd(opcode, subcmd, address, length, aux_address, flags)\n  auto cdb \u003d BuildFtCmd(0xDB, 0x01, 0x1000, 0x20, 0x3000, 0x80);\n\n  ASSERT_EQ(cdb.size(), 16);\n\n  // Verify layout matches FtCmdFormat packed struct inside ft_scsi.cc:\n  // opcode (offset 0)\n  EXPECT_EQ(cdb[0], 0xDB);\n\n  // address (offset 1, 4 bytes, little endian)\n  uint32_t addr \u003d cdb[1] | (cdb[2] \u003c\u003c 8) | (cdb[3] \u003c\u003c 16) | (cdb[4] \u003c\u003c 24);\n  EXPECT_EQ(addr, 0x1000);\n\n  // length (offset 5, 4 bytes, little endian)\n  uint32_t len \u003d cdb[5] | (cdb[6] \u003c\u003c 8) | (cdb[7] \u003c\u003c 16) | (cdb[8] \u003c\u003c 24);\n  EXPECT_EQ(len, 0x20);\n\n  // aux_address (offset 9, 4 bytes, little endian)\n  uint32_t aux \u003d cdb[9] | (cdb[10] \u003c\u003c 8) | (cdb[11] \u003c\u003c 16) | (cdb[12] \u003c\u003c 24);\n  EXPECT_EQ(aux, 0x3000);\n\n  // subcmd (offset 13)\n  EXPECT_EQ(cdb[13], 0x01);\n\n  // flags (offset 14)\n  EXPECT_EQ(cdb[14], 0x80);\n}\n\n}  // namespace\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n  ::testing::InitGoogleTest(\u0026argc, argv);\n  return RUN_ALL_TESTS();\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Update `util/focaltech/build.mk`\n\nAppend the test binary definition to [util/focaltech/build.mk](file:///google/cog/cloud/tomhughes/chromeos-dev2/chrome-internal/src/platform/ec/util/focaltech/build.mk). We include all object files (except `main.o` to avoid `main()` conflicts), proving that the entire tool successfully links against `libusb`, `boringssl`, and `gtest`.\n\n```\n# Register the test binary as a host C++ utility\nhost-util-bin-cxx-y +\u003d focaltech_test\n\n# Define the objects required for the test binary\nfocaltech_test-objs :\u003d $(addprefix $(_cur_dir)/, \\\n\tfocaltech_test.o \\\n\tusb_context.o \\\n\tft_scsi.o \\\n\tupdater.o \\\n)\n\n_focaltech_test_bin :\u003d $(out)/util/focaltech_test\n\n# Configure flags to pull in gtest and gmock via pkg-config\n$(_focaltech_test_bin): HOST_CXXFLAGS+\u003d-fvisibility\u003dhidden -Iutil/focaltech\n$(_focaltech_test_bin): HOST_CXXFLAGS+\u003d$(shell $(HOST_PKG_CONFIG) --cflags libusb-1.0 boringssl gtest gmock)\n$(_focaltech_test_bin): HOST_LDFLAGS+\u003d$(shell $(HOST_PKG_CONFIG) --libs libusb-1.0 boringssl gtest gmock)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Standalone Chroot Verification\n\nVerify the build and test execution directly in your chroot terminal:\n\n1. **Build the host utilities:**\n\n```shell\n(chroot) ~/chromiumos/src/platform/ec $ rm -rf build \u0026\u0026 make BOARD\u003dhost utils-host\n```\n\n2. **Execute the test binary:**\n\n```shell\n(chroot) ~/chromiumos/src/platform/ec $ ./build/host/util/focaltech_test\n```\n\n   You should see standard GoogleTest green output confirming all 4 basic tests passed.",
