      "message": "The vast majority of your casts happen because size variables (`len`, `file_len`, `per_len`) are declared as signed `int`, but the standard library (`std::vector::size()`, `std::span`) and your USB APIs expect unsigned types (`size_t` or `uint32_t`).\n\n**In `updater.cc` (`FtDownloadBin`):**\n\n```c\n// BAD (Current):\nint file_len \u003d buffer.size();\nint len \u003d total_frame * kFocalConfigSize;\nint per_len \u003d kFocalConfigSize;\n\n// GOOD:\nsize_t file_len \u003d buffer.size();\nsize_t len \u003d total_frame * kFocalConfigSize;\nsize_t per_len \u003d kFocalConfigSize;\n\n```\n\n**The Impact:** By making these `size_t`, you completely eliminate the need for functional casts like `size_t(per_len)` and `size_t(len)` when creating spans later in the function.",
