      "message": "This function is very long and complex, which makes it hard to read and maintain.\n\nHere\u0027s Gemini-generated code to fix it. Check for correctness:\n\n----\n\n`UsbDevice::Create` is suffering from \"God Function\" syndrome. It is trying to do too many things at once, violating the Single Responsibility Principle (SRP) and introducing deep, difficult-to-read nesting (the endpoint discovery loop is four levels deep!).\n\nA clean factory method should read like a high-level table of contents. We can drastically simplify this by extracting the heavily nested logic into private static helper functions inside the anonymous namespace of `usb_context.cc`.\n\nHere is how to slice that monolithic function into readable, maintainable pieces.\n\n### Step 1: Extract Device Discovery\n\nPull the iteration over the `libusb` device list into its own helper. This isolates the VID/PID matching logic.\n\n**Add to the anonymous namespace in `usb_context.cc`:**\n\n```cpp\n// Helper to find the specific FocalTech device in the USB tree\nlibusb_device* FindFocalDevice(libusb_device** list, ssize_t count, \n                               libusb_device_descriptor\u0026 out_desc) {\n  for (ssize_t i \u003d 0; i \u003c count; ++i) {\n    libusb_device* dev \u003d list[i];\n    if (libusb_get_device_descriptor(dev, \u0026out_desc) \u003c 0) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    if (out_desc.idVendor \u003d\u003d kFocalBootVid || \n        out_desc.idVendor \u003d\u003d kFocalRomVid ||\n        out_desc.idVendor \u003d\u003d kFocalEcVid) {\n          \n      // Filter out non-fingerprint Google devices\n      if (out_desc.idVendor \u003d\u003d kFocalEcVid \u0026\u0026 \n          (out_desc.idProduct !\u003d kFocalEcPidTest \u0026\u0026\n           out_desc.idProduct !\u003d kFocalEcPid9865 \u0026\u0026\n           out_desc.idProduct !\u003d kFocalEcPid9869)) {\n        LOGI(\"Found Google device {:04x}:{:04x}, but not Focal. Skipping.\",\n             out_desc.idVendor, out_desc.idProduct);\n        continue;\n      }\n      return dev; // Match found\n    }\n  }\n  return nullptr;\n}\n\n```\n\n### Step 2: Extract Endpoint Discovery\n\nThis is the biggest win for readability. Pulling the 4-level deep nested loop out of the main function prevents cognitive overload.\n\n**Add to the anonymous namespace in `usb_context.cc`:**\n\n```cpp\n// Helper to parse the configuration descriptor for bulk IN/OUT endpoints\nbool FindBulkEndpoints(libusb_device* dev, UsbConnectionDetails\u0026 details) {\n  libusb_config_descriptor* config \u003d nullptr;\n  if (libusb_get_config_descriptor(dev, 0, \u0026config) !\u003d LIBUSB_SUCCESS) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  bool found_endpoints \u003d false;\n\n  for (int j \u003d 0; j \u003c config-\u003ebNumInterfaces \u0026\u0026 !found_endpoints; ++j) {\n    const libusb_interface\u0026 interface \u003d config-\u003einterface[j];\n    \n    for (int k \u003d 0; k \u003c interface.num_altsetting \u0026\u0026 !found_endpoints; ++k) {\n      const libusb_interface_descriptor\u0026 alt \u003d interface.altsetting[k];\n      details.interface_num \u003d alt.bInterfaceNumber;\n\n      for (int l \u003d 0; l \u003c alt.bNumEndpoints; ++l) {\n        const libusb_endpoint_descriptor\u0026 ep \u003d alt.endpoint[l];\n        \n        if ((ep.bmAttributes \u0026 LIBUSB_TRANSFER_TYPE_MASK) \u003d\u003d LIBUSB_TRANSFER_TYPE_BULK) {\n          if ((ep.bEndpointAddress \u0026 LIBUSB_ENDPOINT_DIR_MASK) \u003d\u003d LIBUSB_ENDPOINT_IN) {\n            details.ep_bulk_in \u003d ep.bEndpointAddress;\n          } else {\n            details.ep_bulk_out \u003d ep.bEndpointAddress;\n          }\n        }\n      }\n      if (details.ep_bulk_in !\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 details.ep_bulk_out !\u003d 0) {\n        found_endpoints \u003d true;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  \n  libusb_free_config_descriptor(config);\n  return found_endpoints;\n}\n\n```\n\n### Step 3: Rewrite `UsbDevice::Create`\n\nNow, the factory method acts strictly as an orchestrator. It reads sequentially, clearly detailing the steps to establish a connection without getting bogged down in the implementation details.\n\n**Replace the existing `UsbDevice::Create` with this:**\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cUsbDevice, FtError\u003e UsbDevice::Create(\n    const UsbContext\u0026 ctx, UsbConnectionDetails\u0026 out_details) {\n        \n  libusb_device** list_raw \u003d nullptr;\n  ssize_t count \u003d libusb_get_device_list(ctx.get(), \u0026list_raw);\n  if (count \u003c 0) {\n    LOGE(\"Failed to get USB device list: {}\", libusb_error_name(count));\n    return std::unexpected(FtError::kNoSuchDevice);\n  }\n  ScopedDeviceList dev_list(list_raw);\n\n  // 1. Find Device\n  libusb_device_descriptor target_desc{};\n  libusb_device* target_dev \u003d FindFocalDevice(dev_list.get(), count, target_desc);\n  if (!target_dev) {\n    return std::unexpected(FtError::kNoSuchDevice);\n  }\n  \n  out_details.vid \u003d target_desc.idVendor;\n  out_details.pid \u003d target_desc.idProduct;\n  LOGI(\"Found device VID {:04x}: PID {:04x}\", out_details.vid, out_details.pid);\n\n  // 2. Open Handle\n  libusb_device_handle* handle \u003d nullptr;\n  int r \u003d libusb_open(target_dev, \u0026handle);\n  if (r !\u003d LIBUSB_SUCCESS || !handle) {\n    LOGE(\"Failed to open device: {}\", libusb_error_name(r));\n    return std::unexpected(FtError::kNoSuchDevice);\n  }\n  std::unique_ptr\u003clibusb_device_handle, LibusbDeviceHandleDeleter\u003e handle_holder(handle);\n\n  // 3. Find Endpoints\n  if (!FindBulkEndpoints(target_dev, out_details)) {\n    LOGE(\"Could not find required bulk IN/OUT endpoints.\");\n    return std::unexpected(FtError::kNoSuchDevice);\n  }\n\n  // 4. Initialize Connection (Detach, Reset, Claim)\n  if (libusb_kernel_driver_active(handle_holder.get(), out_details.interface_num) \u003d\u003d 1) {\n    if (libusb_detach_kernel_driver(handle_holder.get(), out_details.interface_num) !\u003d LIBUSB_SUCCESS) {\n      LOGE(\"Failed to detach kernel driver.\");\n      return std::unexpected(FtError::kResultFail);\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (libusb_reset_device(handle_holder.get()) \u003c 0) {\n    LOGE(\"Failed to reset the device\");\n    return std::unexpected(FtError::kResultFail);\n  }\n  std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(200)); \n\n  if (libusb_claim_interface(handle_holder.get(), out_details.interface_num) \u003c 0) {\n    LOGE(\"Failed to claim interface.\");\n    return std::unexpected(FtError::kResultFail);\n  }\n\n  // 5. Transfer ownership to the class\n  return UsbDevice(handle_holder.release(), out_details.ep_bulk_in, \n                   out_details.ep_bulk_out, ctx.get());\n}\n\n```",
