      "message": "Here is a Gemini-generated fix. It also changes the argument to use `std::chrono` as we have done elsewhere. Check for correctness:\n\n----\n\n**1\\. Add this private helper to `usb_context.h` (inside `class UsbDevice`):**\n\n```c\n private:\n  // Centralized error recovery for bulk transfers\n  std::expected\u003cint, FtError\u003e HandleTransferError(int libusb_error) const;\n\n```\n\n**2\\. Implement it in `usb_context.cc`:**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cint, FtError\u003e UsbDevice::HandleTransferError(int libusb_error) const {\n  libusb_reset_device(handle_.get());\n  std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(200));\n\n  if (libusb_error \u003d\u003d LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_DEVICE) {\n    return std::unexpected(FtError::kNoSuchDevice);\n  }\n  return std::unexpected(FtError::kResultFail);\n}\n\n```\n\n**3\\. Dramatically simplify `Send` and `Recv` in `usb_context.cc`:**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cint, FtError\u003e UsbDevice::Send(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e buf,\n                                            uint32_t timeout_ms) const {\n  if (!handle_) return std::unexpected(FtError::kNoSuchDevice);\n\n  int actual_len \u003d 0;\n  int r \u003d libusb_bulk_transfer(handle_.get(), endpoint_out_,\n                               const_cast\u003cuint8_t*\u003e(buf.data()),\n                               static_cast\u003cint\u003e(buf.size()), \u0026actual_len, timeout_ms);\n\n  if (r !\u003d LIBUSB_SUCCESS) {\n    return HandleTransferError(r);\n  }\n  return actual_len;\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003cint, FtError\u003e UsbDevice::Recv(std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e buf,\n                                            uint32_t timeout_ms) const {\n  if (!handle_) return std::unexpected(FtError::kNoSuchDevice);\n\n  int actual_len \u003d 0;\n  int r \u003d libusb_bulk_transfer(handle_.get(), endpoint_in_, buf.data(),\n                               static_cast\u003cint\u003e(buf.size()), \u0026actual_len, timeout_ms);\n                               \n  if (r !\u003d LIBUSB_SUCCESS) {\n    return HandleTransferError(r);\n  }\n  return std::min(actual_len, static_cast\u003cint\u003e(buf.size()));\n}\n\n```\n\n*(This makes the core I/O functions vastly easier to read at a glance).*\n\nHere is how you update the call sites in `ft_scsi.cc` and `main.cc` to complete the loop.\n\n### 1\\. Clean Up `util/focaltech/ft_scsi.cc`\n\nSince the `timeout_ms` parameter in `SendBulkDataOut` and `ReceiveBulkDataIn` is already a `std::chrono::milliseconds` object, you no longer have to extract the raw integer with `.count()`. You just pass the time object directly down to the device.\n\n**In the `SendCbw` helper:**\n\n```c\n  // BEFORE:\n  // auto send_res \u003d device.Send(cbw_span, timeout_ms.count());\n\n  // AFTER: Beautifully type-safe.\n  auto send_res \u003d device.Send(cbw_span, timeout_ms);\n\n```\n\n**In the `ReceiveAndValidateCsw` helper:**\n\n```c\n  // BEFORE:\n  // auto recv_res \u003d device.Recv(csw_span, timeout_ms.count());\n\n  // AFTER:\n  auto recv_res \u003d device.Recv(csw_span, timeout_ms);\n\n```\n\n**In `SendBulkDataOut` and `ReceiveBulkDataIn`:**\n\n```c\n  // BEFORE:\n  // auto send_res \u003d device.Send(data_buffer, timeout_ms.count());\n  // auto recv_res \u003d device.Recv(data_buffer, timeout_ms.count());\n\n  // AFTER:\n  auto send_res \u003d device.Send(data_buffer, timeout_ms);\n  \n  // ...\n  \n  auto recv_res \u003d device.Recv(data_buffer, timeout_ms);\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2\\. Clean Up `util/focaltech/main.cc`\n\nIn `main.cc`, we will finally implement those `constexpr` timing constants using C++ chrono literals. This eliminates the magic numbers and makes the generic `SwitchMcuMode` helper we built earlier perfectly safe.\n\n**First, add the constants at the top of `main.cc` (below the includes):**\n\n```c\nusing namespace std::chrono_literals;\n\n// Centralized, strongly-typed timing configurations\nconstexpr auto kFastUsbTimeout \u003d 200ms;\nconstexpr auto kSlowUsbTimeout \u003d 1000ms;\nconstexpr auto kMcuRebootPollInterval \u003d 10ms;\nconstexpr auto kResetWaitTimeout \u003d 3s; \n\n```\n\n**Next, update `CheckEcBuildVersion`:**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, FtError\u003e CheckEcBuildVersion(UsbDevice\u0026 usb,\n                                                 FtDeviceMode current_mode) {\n  // ... \n  \n  for (int attempt \u003d 1; attempt \u003c\u003d kMaxRetry; ++attempt) {\n    // BEFORE: auto sr \u003d usb.Send(kGetBuildVersionCmd, 200);\n    // AFTER: Uses the typed constant directly\n    auto sr \u003d usb.Send(kGetBuildVersionCmd, kFastUsbTimeout);\n    \n    // ...\n    \n    // BEFORE: auto rr \u003d usb.Recv(rx, 1000);\n    // AFTER:\n    auto rr \u003d usb.Recv(rx, kSlowUsbTimeout);\n    \n    // ...\n    \n    // BEFORE: std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(10));\n    // AFTER:\n    std::this_thread::sleep_for(kMcuRebootPollInterval);\n  }\n  \n  // ...\n}\n\n```\n\n**Finally, update our DRY `SwitchMcuMode` helper:**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, FtError\u003e SwitchMcuMode(UsbDevice\u0026 usb, \n                                           FtDeviceMode current_mode,\n                                           std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e switch_cmd,\n                                           std::string_view mode_name) {\n  // ...\n\n  for (int attempt \u003d 1; attempt \u003c\u003d kMaxRetry; ++attempt) {\n    // Look how clean this is compared to the original code!\n    auto sr \u003d usb.Send(switch_cmd, kFastUsbTimeout);\n    // ...\n\n    auto rr \u003d usb.Recv(rx, kFastUsbTimeout);\n    // ...\n\n    std::this_thread::sleep_for(kMcuRebootPollInterval);\n  }\n\n  // Uses the 3s chrono literal constant\n  if (auto res \u003d usb.ResetComplete(kResetWaitTimeout); !res) {\n    return std::unexpected(res.error());\n  }\n  return {};\n}\n\n```",
